{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "checked": "2026-10-08",
  "baseline_commit": "6f2ce7bf",
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Tank and swordman assignments conflict",
      "issue": 683,
      "evidence": "data/re_reference/enemy_ids.json bestiary explicitly identifies tank as Arkzein (source slot 40). Current phobos/phobos_dyna use tank/tank_rare (40/41); arkzein/arkzein_r use swordman/swordman_rare (48/50); zaphobos/zaphobos_dyna use swordman_b/swordman_rare_b (49/51). The saved reference proves the base tank naming conflict but does not establish every swordman or rare display name. User direction on 2026-10-10 remaps Zaphobos/Dyna to tank/tank_rare; this is an explicit game mapping, not a new bestiary identification. Follow-up correction: Phobos/Dyna now use swordman_b/swordman_rare_b as the melee pair.",
      "next": "Recover variant bestiary labels before proposing a complete display-name/ID migration. Use rigs, not current names, for #688/#689 comparisons."
    },
    {
      "title": "Mother family and shrine boss are distinct",
      "issue": 683,
      "evidence": "mother_trinity uses source mother (57), while humilias uses boss_mother (66). The boss roster identifies boss_mother as the z_004 Mother with face parts; humilias boss definition places it in the shrine arena s07z_na1. mother_sword/gun/tech occupy 58–60. These are different source identities; current display names are not a reliable reference key.",
      "next": "Validate regular mother identity in #690 and the shrine boss in #718 before renaming. Heaven’s Mother is an authored composite encounter, not an additional source-table identity."
    },
    {
      "title": "Robot encounter and orphan attack data",
      "issue": 716,
      "evidence": "chaos_mobius resource and boss definition both use boss_robot, but the encounter is in Arca s06z_na1 while the resource lists Paru. FieldPopulation aliases boss_robot_cmb (65) to boss_robot (63). Boss notes describe a combined Arca rig and refer to chaos_mobius_paru; that ID exists only in the attack table, not as a resource or boss definition. Paru’s arena currently documents a Sinow stand-in.",
      "next": "Resolve split/combined identity and arena routing together. Do not count chaos_mobius_paru as a playable validated variant or silently delete its recorded kit."
    },
    {
      "title": "Shinowa and Sinow encounter collision",
      "issue": 713,
      "evidence": "shinowa resource displays Sinow Beat, but sinow_beat has its own resource and rig. The boss encounter keyed sinow_beat loads shinowa. Neither rig occurs in the vendored retail source-ID table; the October 7 viewer inventory also lacks these models. A missing model-table entry does not establish which game supplied shinowa.",
      "next": "Trace imported asset provenance and intended arena identity across #713/#720 before sharing or swapping their behavior."
    },
    {
      "title": "Source coverage and additions",
      "issue": 683,
      "evidence": "All nonempty retail source names except sample, boss_robot_cmb and boss_mother_piece have a resource model match. sample and the empty slot are not playable; combined robot is aliased; Mother pieces lack standalone resources. Four PSO additions (Poison Lily, Chaos Sorcerer, Sinow Beat/Gold) and unresolved shinowa sit outside this source table. This is table coverage, not proof that every original encounter or boss part is implemented.",
      "next": "Keep source exclusions visible. #718 must verify whether Mother parts are actually implemented; a FieldPopulation comment saying they are boss-owned is not runtime proof."
    }
  ],
